<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
<meta charset="utf-8">
<title>Data Quality Assessment — {{ name }}</title>
<style>
  @page { size: A4; margin: 18mm 16mm 20mm 16mm;
    @bottom-center { content: "Data Quality Assessment · " counter(page) " of " counter(pages);
      font-family: Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 8pt; color: #7A858E; } }
  body { font-family: Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif; color: #24303A; font-size: 10pt; line-height: 1.45; }
  h1 { font-size: 22pt; margin: 0 0 4pt; }
  h2 { font-size: 13pt; margin: 22pt 0 6pt; padding-bottom: 4pt; border-bottom: 1px solid #D8DEE4; }
  h3 { font-size: 11pt; margin: 14pt 0 4pt; }
  .sub { color: #5A6572; font-size: 10pt; margin: 0 0 18pt; }
  .brand { margin: 0 0 16pt; }
  .brand img { height: 26pt; width: auto; display: block; }
  .cover { border-left: 4px solid #3D6B54; padding-left: 14pt; margin-bottom: 20pt; }
  .kpis { display: table; width: 100%; margin: 14pt 0; border-spacing: 6pt 0; }
  .kpi { display: table-cell; width: 25%; background: #F4F6F8; padding: 10pt; border-radius: 4pt; }
  .kpi .v { font-size: 17pt; font-weight: bold; display: block; }
  .kpi .l { font-size: 8pt; color: #5A6572; text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: 0.04em; }
  .score-big { font-size: 40pt; font-weight: bold; line-height: 1; }
  table { width: 100%; border-collapse: collapse; margin: 8pt 0 14pt; font-size: 9pt; }
  th { text-align: left; background: #F4F6F8; padding: 5pt 7pt; border-bottom: 1px solid #D8DEE4; font-size: 8pt;
       text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: 0.03em; color: #5A6572; }
  td { padding: 5pt 7pt; border-bottom: 1px solid #EDF0F3; vertical-align: top; }
  td.num { text-align: right; font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums; }
  .healthy { color: #2F7A55; } .needs { color: #B5761F; } .critical { color: #B33A3A; }
  .na { color: #7A858E; font-style: italic; }
  .bar { height: 7pt; background: #EDF0F3; border-radius: 3pt; overflow: hidden; width: 100%; }
  .bar span { display: block; height: 100%; }
  .note { background: #F4F6F8; border-left: 3px solid #9AA7B1; padding: 8pt 10pt; font-size: 9pt;
          color: #4A5560; margin: 12pt 0; }
  .dim { page-break-inside: avoid; margin-bottom: 16pt; }
  .ex { font-family: "DejaVu Sans Mono", monospace; font-size: 8pt; }
  .page-break { page-break-before: always; }
</style>
</head>
<body>

{% macro cls(b) %}{% if b == 'healthy' %}healthy{% elif b == 'needs attention' %}needs{% elif b == 'critical' %}critical{% else %}na{% endif %}{% endmacro %}
{% macro colour(s) %}{% if s >= 90 %}#2F7A55{% elif s >= 70 %}#B5761F{% else %}#B33A3A{% endif %}{% endmacro %}
{% macro ranked_table(rows) %}
<table>
  <tr><th>Area</th><th class="num">Score</th><th class="num">Failures</th><th>Consequence if unaddressed</th></tr>
  {% for d in rows %}
  <tr>
    <td><strong>{{ d.label }}</strong></td>
    {% if d.score is not none %}
    <td class="num {{ cls(d.band) }}">{{ d.score }}</td>
    <td class="num">{{ "{:,}".format(d.failed) }}</td>
    <td>{{ d.impact }}</td>
    {% else %}
    <td class="num na">not assessed</td>
    <td class="num na">&mdash;</td>
    <td class="na">{{ d.not_assessed }}</td>
    {% endif %}
  </tr>
  {% endfor %}
</table>
{% endmacro %}

<div class="brand"><img src="{{ logo_src }}" alt="DataSkate"></div>

<div class="cover">
  <h1>Data Quality Assessment</h1>
  <p class="sub">{{ name }} · Salesforce {{ environment }} · {{ generated }}</p>
</div>

<h2>Overall result</h2>
<p><span class="score-big {{ cls(overall_band) }}">{{ overall if overall is not none else '—' }}</span>
   <span style="font-size:12pt;color:#5A6572;"> / 100 · {{ overall_band }}</span></p>

<div class="kpis">
  <div class="kpi"><span class="v">{{ "{:,}".format(records) }}</span><span class="l">Records assessed</span></div>
  <div class="kpi"><span class="v">{{ objects_completed }} of {{ objects_selected }}</span><span class="l">Objects assessed</span></div>
  <div class="kpi"><span class="v">{{ cdes }}</span><span class="l">Critical data elements</span></div>
  <div class="kpi"><span class="v">{{ dimensions_scored }}</span><span class="l">Dimensions scored</span></div>
</div>

{% if failed_objects %}
<div class="note"><strong>Partial assessment.</strong> The overall result covers
{{ objects_completed }} of {{ objects_selected }} selected objects. Not assessed:
{% for f in failed_objects %}{{ f.label }} — {{ f.error }}{% if not loop.last %}; {% endif %}{% endfor %}</div>
{% endif %}

<h2>What this means</h2>
{% if any_assessed %}
<p>Every dimension across all assessed objects, weakest first, with the
business consequence of leaving it unaddressed. Dimensions that could not be
assessed on any object are listed last with the reason.</p>
{% endif %}
{{ ranked_table(ranked) }}

<div class="note">The overall result treats the assessed objects as one
dataset: each dimension score is the pass rate across every rule of every
object. An object therefore weighs in proportion to how much of it was
checked, and a small object in poor shape can sit behind a healthy overall
score. The per-object results below show each one on its own.</div>

<h2>Objects assessed</h2>
<table>
  <tr><th>Object</th><th class="num">Records</th><th class="num">Critical fields</th><th class="num">Score</th><th>Weakest area</th></tr>
  {% for o in objects %}
  <tr>
    <td><strong>{{ o.label }}</strong></td>
    <td class="num">{{ "{:,}".format(o.ctx.records) }}</td>
    <td class="num">{{ o.ctx.cdes }} of {{ o.ctx.columns }}</td>
    <td class="num {{ cls(o.ctx.overall_band) }}">{{ o.ctx.overall if o.ctx.overall is not none else '—' }}</td>
    <td>{% if o.weakest %}{{ o.weakest.label }} ({{ o.weakest.score }}){% else %}—{% endif %}</td>
  </tr>
  {% endfor %}
</table>

{% for o in objects %}
{# Each object after the first starts a page. Not the first: the objects
   table above can spill onto a new page, and breaking again would leave
   that page nearly empty. #}
{% if not loop.first %}<div class="page-break"></div>{% endif %}
<h2>{{ o.label }} — {{ o.ctx.overall if o.ctx.overall is not none else '—' }} / 100</h2>
<p class="sub" style="margin-bottom:8pt;">{{ "{:,}".format(o.ctx.records) }} records ·
{{ o.ctx.cdes }} of {{ o.ctx.columns }} fields assessed as critical data elements</p>

{{ ranked_table(o.ctx.ranked) }}

{% if is_in_depth %}
{% for d in o.ctx.dimensions %}{% if d.rules and not d.not_assessed %}
<div class="dim">
  <h3>{{ d.label }} <span class="{{ cls(d.band) }}">— {{ d.score }} / 100</span></h3>
  <table>
    <tr><th>Rule</th><th>Column</th><th class="num">Pass rate</th><th class="num">Failed</th></tr>
    {% for r in d.rules[:rules_shown] %}
    <tr>
      <td>{{ r.rule_name }}</td>
      <td>{{ r.column or 'whole record' }}</td>
      <td class="num">{{ "%.1f%%" | format(r.passRate * 100) }}</td>
      <td class="num">{{ "{:,}".format(r.failed) }}</td>
    </tr>
    {% endfor %}
  </table>
</div>
{% endif %}{% endfor %}

{% for d in o.ctx.dimensions %}{% for ex in d.examples %}
<h3>{{ o.label }} · {{ d.label }} — {{ ex.rule.rule_name }}</h3>
<table class="ex">
  <tr><th>Row</th><th>Column</th><th>Value</th><th>Issue</th></tr>
  {% for row in ex.rows %}
  <tr><td class="num">{{ row.row }}</td><td>{{ row.column or '—' }}</td>
      <td>{{ row.value }}</td><td>{{ row.reason }}</td></tr>
  {% endfor %}
</table>
{% endfor %}{% endfor %}
{% endif %}
{% endfor %}

<h2>Limitations</h2>
<p>Each object was assessed as the Salesforce Run As user sees it: objects
and fields that user cannot read were not downloaded. Relationships between
objects — whether a Contact's Account exists, for instance — were not
checked in this assessment. Accuracy is assessed without an external source
of truth: it covers reference-list conformance, cross-field contradiction
and statistical outliers, and cannot confirm that a plausible value is
factually correct.</p>

</body>
</html>
